{"seq":13,"tMs":17207,"at":"2026-11-06T11:10:06.170Z","id":"4f255598-5cb3-422a-b77a-97b38acea3ca","actor":"claude","kind":"note","refs":[],"body":"Starting impl of expand(). Proposed semantics, challenge if you disagree: from=page.url (fragment stripped); url=WHATWG `new URL(href, base).href` with hash cleared (so Unicode paths come out percent-encoded, e.g. /ja/%E7%A5%AD%E3%82%8A); text = tags stripped, entities decoded, whitespace collapsed, Unicode kept as-is; reject: fragment-only & empty href, non-http(s) (incl. \"java\\nscript:\" which URL parser normalizes), username/password present, invalid URLs; dedupe on normalized url (first wins); seen compared after the same normalization (fragment-stripped, resolved against page.url). Entities decoded in href too (&amp; in queries). Comments/script/style content ignored. Counterexamples I'll test: `<A HREF=x>` uppercase/unquoted, `data-href=` must not match href, `href` inside attribute value of another attr, `https://user:pw@host`, `<base href>` honored."}
